course: dictionary
lesson: 6575
title: Nightly: every night
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Nightly» comes from «night», and it tells you how often something happens: once each night. Read this: «The arguments did not vanish, but they shrank from a nightly war to the odd grumble.» A nightly war is a fight that happens every night.
explain: Check the clues around the word. «The odd grumble» means a complaint now and then, which is the opposite of a nightly war. So nightly means regular and frequent, with the same thing happening over and over.
explain: Nightly can also mean happening at night, as in nightly prayers. Swap your meaning into the sentence: «a every-night war» still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Nightly means happening every night, once each night.
fact: «Twice nightly» means two times every night.
fact: Something that happens nightly happens 7 times in a week.
fact: Nightly can also mean happening at night, as in «nightly prayers».
fact: «The nightly news» is the news shown on television every evening.
exercise: «The arguments shrank from a nightly war to the odd grumble.» What does nightly mean here? | Only at lunchtime | *Every night | Very loud | Once a year
exercise: A street light is switched on nightly. How many times is it switched on in one week? | 24 times | 14 times | 1 time | *7 times
exercise: Zara's dad reads her a story nightly. How often does he read to her? | Never | *Every night | Only on holidays | Once a week
test: The fox came nightly to the bins. What does nightly tell you? | It came only when it snowed | *It came every night | It never came | It came once at dawn
test: Twice nightly means how many times each night? | *Two | Zero | Seven | One
exam: Nightly means how often? | Happening only in the morning | Happening only on Sundays | Happening once a year | *Happening every night
